.Sh DESCRIPTION
These are the coreutils applets of BusyBox 1.36.1 as built for Rach2.
The os-real image and installed root use these applets.
.Pp
The os-simple image instead uses the project's teaching implementations of
.Nm true ,
.Nm false ,
.Nm echo ,
.Nm yes ,
.Nm cat ,
.Nm pwd ,
.Nm touch ,
.Nm mkdir ,
.Nm rm ,
.Nm mv ,
.Nm cp ,
and
.Nm ls .
They parse no options except
.Nm rm Fl r .
That
.Nm cat
reports open and write failures with status 1, completes short writes,
and treats read errors as end of input.
An open failure skips that operand; a write returning zero or an error
stops the copy.
Close errors do not affect the status.
That
.Nm cp
requires exactly two operands identifying different files.
It truncates the destination without checking file identity, so identical
paths, hard links, and symlink aliases can erase the source.
A missing destination is created with mode 0666 subject to the process umask.
Usage, open, and write failures return status 1; read errors end the copy
silently, and close errors do not affect the status.
That
.Nm rm Fl r
unlinks symbolic links without following their targets.
After an unlink failure, it recurses only if
.Fn lstat
identifies a directory.
It skips a child when the parent length plus one plus the name length
reaches 256, even if the parent ends in a slash.
Directory read errors end traversal silently, and close errors are ignored.
A failed removal returns status 1 and may leave some entries removed.
That
.Nm ls
lists one directory without calling
.Fn stat .
.Bl -tag -width sha256sum
.It Nm arch
Print the system architecture.
.It Nm base32
Encode or decode
.Ar FILE
as base32, writing to standard output.
.It Nm base64
Encode or decode
.Ar FILE
as base64, writing to standard output.
.It Nm basename
Remove the directory path and an optional
.Ar SUFFIX
from
.Ar FILE .
.It Nm cat
Print files to standard output.
.It Nm chgrp
Change the group of files to
.Ar GROUP .
.It Nm chmod
Change file modes.
.Ar MODE
is an octal number with bit pattern
.Ql sstrwxrwxrwx ,
or a symbolic mode of the form
.Ql [ugoa]{+|-|=}[rwxXst] .
.It Nm chown
Change the owner or group of files to
.Ar USER
or
.Ar GRP .
.It Nm chroot
Make
.Ar NEWROOT
the root directory and the working directory, as
.Xr chroot 2
describes, and run
.Ar PROG
with
.Ar ARGS
from the new root, or with no
.Ar PROG
a shell with
.Fl i :
.Ev SHELL
when it is set and not empty, else the shell the caller's real user ID
has in the new root's
.Pa /etc/passwd ,
else
.Pa /bin/sh .
.It Nm cksum
Calculate CRC32 checksums of files.
.It Nm comm
Compare
.Ar FILE1
with
.Ar FILE2 .
.It Nm cp
Copy sources to
.Ar DEST
or
.Ar DIRECTORY .
.It Nm crc32
Calculate CRC32 checksums of files.
.It Nm cut
Print selected fields from files to standard output.
.It Nm date
Display the time using
.Ar +FMT ,
or set the time.
Rach2 does not implement the
.Fn clock_settime
system call, so setting the time fails.
.It Nm dd
Copy a file with conversion and formatting.
.It Nm df
Print file system usage statistics.
.It Nm dirname
Remove the last path component from
.Ar FILENAME .
.It Nm dos2unix
Convert
.Ar FILE
in place from DOS to Unix text format.
With no file, use standard input and standard output.
.It Nm du
Summarize the disk space used by files and directories.
.It Nm echo
Print arguments to standard output.
.It Nm env
Print the environment or run
.Ar PROG
with the specified environment.
.It Nm expand
Convert tabs to spaces and write to standard output.
.It Nm expr
Print the value of
.Ar EXPRESSION .
.It Nm factor
Print prime factors.
.It Nm false
Return exit status 1.
.It Nm fold
Wrap lines from files or standard input and write to standard output.
.It Nm fsync
Write buffered file data to disk.
The scope of the write is described in
.Xr sync 2 .
.It Nm groups
Print the groups to which
.Ar USER
belongs.
.It Nm head
Print the first 10 lines of each file, or of standard input.
With more than one file, precede each with a file name header.
.It Nm hostid
Print the machine's 32-bit host identifier.
The musl implementation returns zero; this is not a unique machine identifier.
.It Nm id
Print information about
.Ar USER ,
or about the current user.
.It Nm install
Copy files and set their attributes.
.It Nm link
Create a hard link
.Ar LINK
to
.Ar FILE .
.It Nm ln
Create
.Ar LINK ,
or a link in
.Ar DIR ,
to each
.Ar TARGET .
.It Nm logname
Print the
.Ev LOGNAME
environment variable, which musl's login-name lookup reads; the applet
fails when it is unset or longer than its buffer.
.It Nm ls
List directory contents.
.It Nm md5sum
Print or check MD5 checksums.
.It Nm mkdir
Create directories.
.It Nm mkfifo
Create a named pipe.
Rach2 does not implement the required
.Fn mknod
system call, so creation fails.
.It Nm mknod
Create a block device, character device, or named pipe.
Rach2 does not implement the required
.Fn mknod
system call, so creation fails.
.It Nm mktemp
Create a temporary file using
.Ar TEMPLATE
and print its name.
The template must end in
.Ql XXXXXX .
Without a template,
.Fl t Ar tmp.XXXXXX
is assumed.
The base directory is selected by
.Fl p ,
then
.Ev TMPDIR ,
then
.Pa /tmp .
.It Nm mv
Rename
.Ar SOURCE
to
.Ar DEST ,
or move sources to
.Ar DIRECTORY .
.It Nm nice
Request a scheduling priority adjustment and run
.Ar PROG .
Rach2 does not implement
.Fn getpriority
or
.Fn setpriority .
The failed priority change terminates the applet before it runs
.Ar PROG .
.It Nm nl
Print files with line numbers.
.It Nm nohup
Run
.Ar PROG
with hangup signals ignored and output directed to a nonterminal.
.It Nm nproc
Print the number of processors the caller may run on, which
.Fn sched_getaffinity
gives.
.It Nm od
Display file contents in the selected format.
.It Nm paste
Join lines from input files, separating them with tabs.
.It Nm printenv
Print the specified environment variables, or all variables if none are specified.
.It Nm printf
Format and print arguments according to
.Ar FORMAT ,
as in C printf.
.It Nm pwd
Print the full path of the current working directory.
.It Nm readlink
Print the value of a symbolic link.
.It Nm realpath
Print absolute paths of files.
.It Nm rm
Remove files.
.It Nm rmdir
Remove empty directories.
.It Nm seq
Print numbers from
.Ar FIRST
to
.Ar LAST
in steps of
.Ar INC .
.Ar FIRST
and
.Ar INC
default to 1.
.It Nm sha1sum
Print or check SHA1 checksums.
.It Nm sha256sum
Print or check SHA256 checksums.
.It Nm sha3sum
Print or check SHA3 checksums.
.It Nm sha512sum
Print or check SHA512 checksums.
.It Nm shred
Overwrite or remove files.
.It Nm shuf
Randomly reorder lines.
.It Nm sleep
Sleep for the sum of the given times.
Each argument may have a suffix s for seconds, m for minutes, h for hours, or d for days.
Rach2 sleeps in ticks of 10 ms.
.It Nm sort
Sort lines of text.
.It Nm split
Split input into files with a common
.Ar PREFIX .
.It Nm stat
Display file status, or file system status with
.Fl f .
Under
.Pa /dev ,
